@knowledge

Purpose:
  Newly learned knowledge from tasks and projects.
  Knowledge lifecycle: observe → extract → normalize → classify →
  validate → promote → reference.

Owns: ./

Directories:
  candidates:
    path: ./candidates
    purpose: Unvalidated knowledge candidates

  lessons:
    path: ./lessons
    purpose: Validated lessons learned from tasks

Lifecycle:
  OBSERVE
    ↓
  EXTRACT
    ↓
  NORMALIZE
    ↓
  CLASSIFY
    ↓
  COMPARE
    ↓
  VALIDATE
    ↓
  PROMOTE
    ↓
  LINK
    ↓
  USE
    ↓
  REVIEW
    ↓
  LEARN AGAIN

  KnowledgeValidation:
    source: anthropics/skills skill-creator eval harness
    definition: Quality gate for skills via with-skill vs without-skill A/B testing
    components:
      EvalDefinition:
        source: skills/skill-creator/references/schemas.md
        structure: name, tests[], grading[], metrics[]
        rule: every skill test MUST have at least one assertion

      SubagentExecution:
        source: skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md
        pattern: spawn two subagents per test case in parallel
          - with-skill (skill activated + test prompt)
          - without-skill (baseline, test prompt only)
        rule: subagents run in isolated context windows

      GraderAgent:
        source: skills/skill-creator/agents/grader.md
        role: evaluates assertions, extracts implicit claims
        output: grading.json (assertion -> passed/fail + evidence)
        rule: grader NEVER sees which variant produced which output (blind)

      ComparatorAgent:
        source: skills/skill-creator/agents/comparator.md
        role: unbiased comparison of with-skill vs without-skill outputs
        rule: comparator does NOT know which output came from which variant

      PostHocAnalyzer:
        source: skills/skill-creator/agents/analyzer.md
        role: unblinds results + diagnoses why winner won
        output: analysis.json (patterns, regressions, recommendations)

      BenchmarkAggregation:
        source: skills/skill-creator/scripts/aggregate_benchmark.py
        rule: benchmark.json persists test results across skill versions
        rule: improvement tracked as test_score delta, not train_score

      DescriptionOptimizer:
        source: skills/skill-creator/scripts/improve_description.py
        rule: optimize trigger_description for test score (not train score)
        rule: stratified train/test split prevents overfitting
        rule: each query run 3x for reliability

    QualityGate:
      min_score: 0.8 (80% assertion pass rate vs baseline)
      min_improvement: 0.2 (20% improvement over without-skill baseline)
      min_confidence: 0.7 (70% confidence across runs)
      rule: skills below quality gate are NOT recommended
      rule: human can override promotion below grade with justification
      rule: eval results cached for 30 days (re-run on skill change)

    Integration:
      trigger: .sdd/INDEX.sdd ReadOrder step 6 (@skills)
      storage: eval results -> .sdd/knowledge/candidates/skills/<skill_id>/
      retention: eval cached 30 days; re-run on .sdd or skill file change
      observability: OBS20 (skill_eval_completed) with score + recommendation

  ValidationLifecycle:
    candidates -> validate (via KnowledgeValidation) -> lessons (if validated)
    rule: promotion requires KnowledgeValidation pass
    rule: skills MUST pass eval harness before promotion to validated knowledge

Rules:
  [K1] Every task MAY produce knowledge candidates.
  [K2] Candidates MUST be validated before promotion.
  [K3] Promoted knowledge MUST be linked to references/.
  [K4] Lessons MUST include source task ID.
  [K5] Knowledge MUST be classified by domain.
  [K6] Conflicting knowledge MUST be flagged.
  [K7] Obsolete knowledge MUST be deprecated, not deleted.
  [K8] AI MUST NOT auto-promote without validation.

Navigation:
  Candidates: @candidates/
  Lessons: @lessons/
  References: @../references/INDEX.sdd
  Insights: @../insights/INDEX.sdd

State: +
